      "writtenOn": "2025-03-11T10:35:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It\u0027s true that this check isn\u0027t cheap, but `ComputeChecksum` is only called at compile time, so I think it\u0027s fine. Yes, we do care about compile time cost, but optimizing this check doesn\u0027t really help much. Besides, reordering the fields also has a compile time cost, which may be the same or even higher.\n\nIMO, if we\u0027d like to optimize anything, I\u0027d start with optimizing `GetStoreValueByKey`, because it\u0027s not cheap either (it\u0027s a lookup in O(n) time) and it\u0027s called multiple times **at runtime**.\n\nFor now, I\u0027d suggest to leave `ComputeChecksum` as is.",
